@{
    ViewData["Title:"] = "Blog/Reflection";
}

<div class="container mt-5">
    <h2 class="mb-4">Reflection on the Activity</h2>

    <p>
        While working on this activity, I learned how to setup a database, know how to use SSMS and set it up. 
        It was confusing at first but got the hang of it by browsing through the web and for help of friends.
        Other than that, this activity help me know how to add tooltips, navigation buttons,
        and modify the routing so that the application’s default page goes directly to the
        Records view instead of the Index page.
    </p>

    <p>
        Setting up the DevController with its own Index view was also a good learning moment for me.
        It showed me how ASP.NET Core keeps controllers and views neatly paired in their own folders,
        which makes the project easier to manage and less confusing when it grows bigger.
    </p>

    <p>
        Overall, this activity not only taught me new technical skills but also gave me a better
        sense of how small improvements in design and navigation can really change the overall
        experience of using the app. It made me appreciate the little touches that make a project
        feel complete.
    </p>

</div>
